dfw (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * When a rule names a container that uses another container's network
    (--network container:NAME, or compose's network_mode: service:NAME),
    the warning now says whose network it uses, and so whose rules it
    gets, and which name to use instead.

 -- dfw maintainers <lookap.dev@gmail.com>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:40:24 +0100

dfw (0.1.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rules accept address ranges, such as 10.0.0.5-10.0.0.20 or
    [fd00::1-fd00::ff]:443. A range must lie wholly inside or wholly
    outside each private and special block.
  * Security: a compose service name now matches only containers named the
    way Compose names them, <project>-<service>-<N>. An image could set the
    com.docker.compose.* labels itself and claim another service's rules.
    dfw check warns when a rule names a service that such a container
    claims.

 -- dfw maintainers <lookap.dev@gmail.com>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:36:51 +0100

dfw (0.1.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * dfw check lists the containers under each network by name.

 -- dfw maintainers <lookap.dev@gmail.com>  Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:22:37 +0100

dfw (0.1.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New zone any: every IPv4 and IPv6 address. allow [foo] -> any gives a
    container the outbound access it has without dfw.
  * README.md and dfw(8) document # comments in the rules files.

 -- dfw maintainers <lookap.dev@gmail.com>  Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:38:36 +0100

dfw (0.1.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * dfw enable refuses to run on a kernel without nft_meta_bridge or
    nf_conntrack_bridge, such as Raspberry Pi OS's, naming the missing
    modules, and dfw check reports them as an error.
  * dfw check lists each network's containers under it, and the rules one
    line per peer with the ports it reaches.

 -- dfw maintainers <lookap.dev@gmail.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:19:24 +0100

dfw (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A running container that Docker fails to answer about keeps its rules,
    instead of being blocked and having its connections cut.

 -- dfw maintainers <lookap.dev@gmail.com>  Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:30:07 +0100

dfw (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: a bridge-level nftables firewall for the containers on
    chosen Docker networks, with allow rules in /etc/dfw/rules and
    /etc/dfw/rules.d. See README.md and dfw(8).

 -- dfw maintainers <lookap.dev@gmail.com>  Sun, 08 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
